feat(reconciler): fill pool-under-min demand by exact key (D-WAKE part 2)

detectorActWakePoolFill flips, which crosses D-WAKE's last two arms:

  - the slotized pool member's re-wake routes through the SAME certified-lease
    entry its named/dependency siblings use (AdmitStrictDefaultPoolWake), whose
    legacy yield already existed in sessionStartLegacyExclusionPredicate;
  - the pool-under-min FILL - the family's one arm with no session row, because
    the member does not exist yet - routes its exact
    (workID, poolTarget, sourceStore) key into the pool-allocation admission,
    whose legacy yield is the allocation-ownership seam landed in the previous
    commit.

detectPoolFill reads only what the tick already carries: the desired counts
ComputePoolDesiredStates precomputed, and the promoted routed-work view's
unallocated entries. Open members are counted the way the pool planner counts
them, so demand a member has already spent is never re-raised, and the arm
accrues its own fills so one sweep never overfills a pool short by one.

The ready-demand scan is now ABSORBED rather than inventoried: Q2 resolved
yes-with-promotion, so detectorFamilyReadyDemandScan and its act constant
retire - the sweep owns the read, so there is no foreign scan left to observe.

REDs (cmd/gc/session_detector_pool_fill_test.go):

  - FillsPoolUnderMinByExactKey: the primary - under-filled pool + unallocated
    routed work => one start-candidate with no session key, handed to the
    pool-allocation admission under its exact key
  - StartsARealSession: the AC's upgrade of the request-count-only legacy
    assertion - the key the sweep produced, driven through the unchanged
    handler, materializes a member with a new instance token, the routed
    trigger, and exactly one live provider Start
  - NeverFillsPoolAtOrAboveMin (negative): a filled pool is never enqueued and
    starts nothing however much work waits
  - NeverOverfillsOneSweep: a pool short by one gets one member, not three
  - OverflowIsCensusOwedAndRefills (negative): a saturated channel drops the
    hint, the seam records refused_overflow and returns - no retry, no block,
    no legacy fallback, not counted as keyed-owned - and the NEXT sweep
    re-detects the same durable condition and fills it
  - RefusesWithoutAnAdmissionSeam: a keyed city with no pool-allocation
    admission records the traced refusal and enqueues nothing

Act-frontier repin: the D-WAKE reason frontier now lists all three routing
arms, and the FILL arm is pinned to claim NO session-start admission source.
This was D-WAKE's last family arm - the act map is complete.

